  "answer": "Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L348-L350`. - 2. [implemented] Resolve the permission mode from `--mode`, else `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE`, else `ask`, and build a dispatcher for it. [3] Common options on the acting subcommands: - [implemented] `--mode` selects the permission mode (read-only, ask, auto-safe, environment-scoped, bypass); when omitted, `run` and `fix` read `PRASH_PERMISSION_MODE` from the credentials file and fall back to `ask`. [1]",
